1.11
====
- add workaround for PMIC overvoltage bug

  -- 2026-06-25

1.10.1
======
- spi gpio: remember mode per adapter

  -- 2026-06-19

1.10
====
- spi: support SPI_CPHA, SPI_CPOL, and SPI_CS_HIGH

  -- 2026-06-17

1.9
===
- no need to reset if booting from ONOFF button
Since resetting was pointless, the reset process was reverted, leaving the flag
clearing intact. Both booting from ONOFF button and reset by PMIC_Reset() result
in a POR boot.

  -- 2026-04-17

1.8
===
- tty/lpuart: add new settermios srtm API.
This allows setting baud rate to non-standard values as supported by
the driver.
- slightly improve hardfault handler: log stack frame if available
and increase delay after boot from 30 to 40s

  -- 2026-01-23

1.7
===
- rtc: fix boot from ONOFF signal (clear leftover BBNSM irq)
- add poweroff from uboot

  -- 2025-11-06

1.6
===
- srtm_rtc: new service for RTC over rpmsg
- tty/lpuart_1wire: fix '0x00' bogus receives when transmitting
- make release build more reproducible. Builds with SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH
set and identical toolchain should now be identical.

  -- 2025-10-21

1.5
===
- tty/lpuart: fix bug on suspend with tty open
- tty/lpuart_1wire: add one-wire mode based on lpuart
- tty/lpuart: add control hook for tcsendbreak

  -- 2025-09-22

1.4
===
- spi/lpspi: fix to properly use lpspi's mode on init (instead of different union value)
- tty/flexio: fix memory leak on setcflag
- pwm: add TPM2/3 support
- pwm: improve setting precision (do not round to 1%)

  -- 2025-07-29

1.3
===
- BREAKING (linux rpmsg compat): rpmsg spi protocol update
A new (common) init field was added so protocol version was updated,
and m33 update will require a linux update.
- spi: implement lpspi for spi[0-3]
- suspend: implement underdrive control for m33 core, and add a new
'active_ud' mode to automatically enter underdrive when linux sleeps
- suspend/wdog: implement m33-side wdog handover for when linux suspend
in active* mode
- wdog: refactor out of app_srtm.c and implement wdog for uboot, so
failure to boot linux will reset
- hardfault handler: implement minimum uboot protocol handling to
allow uboot relocation and rollback in case of early hardfault
- custom: add more custom hooks for easier prototyping
- gpio: refactor with custom consumers in mind.
- suspend: fix suspend in deep sleep for >24h. This used to require
a hard reset because the sentinel wdog timer apparently was not suspended
during deep sleep.

  -- 2025-06-23

1.2
===
- dac/audio services
- flexio support baudrate change
- (mostly) fix A core voltage not being lowered during suspend

  -- 2025-05-26

1.1.1
===========
- add spi rpmsg implementation
- only log wdog ping once after init (boot/resume)
- fix rare reboot loop on sd boot (secure enclave reset loop)

  -- 2025-04-14

